  "text": "Veterinary Oncology | Pet Cancer Care | Davies Vet Specialists\nPet Owners\n>\nMeet Our Team\nBeing referred to Davies\nFacilities\nThe Referral Process\nFact Sheets\nFAQ\nClient Care\nFinance and Insurance\nSustainability\nVet Professionals\n>\nAppointment Request Form\nEmergency Referrals\nRadiology Request Form\nTPLO Post Op Form\nBook CPD\nCPD Webinar Library\nPopular Downloads\nServices\n>\nAnaesthesia\nCardiology\nDentistry & Maxillofacial Surgery\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency and Critical Care\nHearing Assessment Clinic\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology\nNursing\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nOrthopaedics\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nTherapy Services\nClient Care\nOur Team\n>\nAnaesthesia Team\nCardiology Team\nClient Care Team\nDentistry & Maxillofacial Surgery Team\nDermatology Team\nEmergency & Critical Care Team\nDiagnostic Imaging Team\nGreen Group\nHearing Clinic Team\nFinance Team\nInternal Medicine Team\nInterns\nLeadership Team\nNeurology Team\nNursing Team\nOncology Team\nOphthalmology Team\nOrthopaedics Team\nPain Management Team\nPatient Care Assistants and Technicians\nTherapy Services Team\nSoft Tissue Surgery Team\nSupport Team\nJoin Our Team\nContact Us\nInsights\n>\nBlogs\nNews\nFact Sheets\nCase Studies\nNewsletters\nCPD\nEmergencies\n01582 883950\nRefer Here\nLog In / Register\nUPDATE: Please be aware that our opening hours have changed on Monday 19th September. Please contact us for any emergency care.\nVeterinary Oncology\nIf your pet has been referred to us with a cancer diagnosis, rest assured we understand that it can be a frightening and confusing time. We are here to help. Pet owners often have many choices to make regarding possible treatments. Talking to owners about their pet’s disease and guiding them through difficult choices is a core part of our oncologists’ roles.\nVeterinary Oncology: The diagnosis, management and treatment of\ncancer in cats and dogs.\nWe know a cancer diagnosis for your pet can be incredibly upsetting. At Davies Veterinary Specialists, our oncology team is here to provide compassionate support every step of the way. We focus on preserving your pet’s quality of life, offering comprehensive care from diagnosis and treatment to palliative support, allowing them to enjoy as much of a normal life as possible.\nDiagnosing Cancer & Planning Treatment in our Veterinary Oncology Department\nAt Davies Veterinary Specialists, our multidisciplinary approach ensures your pet receives a swift and accurate cancer diagnosis using the least invasive methods. Our advanced on-site imaging, including CT, MRI, and ultrasound, facilitates rapid diagnosis and staging. Our oncology service benefits from the expertise of European Veterinary Specialists in\nanaesthesia,\nneurology\n,\northopaedics\n,\nand\nsoft tissue surgery\n, enabling us to perform complex cancer surgeries, from thoracic and abdominal procedures to specialised oral and spinal surgeries. Our long-standing\nchemotherapy\nclinic, led by skilled nurses and oncologists, provides personalised and compassionate care. We treat a wide range of cancers, offering\nchemotherapy\nas a standalone treatment or in combination with surgery and radiotherapy.\nPrioritising Quality of Life with Veterinary Oncology Treatment\nThe philosophy of our\npet oncology service\nis to ensure every pet we see maintains the best quality of life during treatment. In many cases, combinations of medical and surgical treatment can have very positive outcomes on quality of life. We are also able to treat cancer through various means, including drugs (chemotherapy and tyrosine kinase inhibitors), the melanoma vaccine (Oncept) therapy,\nElectrochemotherapy\nand surgery. The diagnosis and treatment of cancer requires input from other disciplines within the hospital, so our oncologists work very closely with soft tissue surgeons and other clinical services teams.\nSupporting Your pets with Palliative Care Services\nMaintaining your pet’s comfort and well-being is paramount throughout their cancer journey. Our\noncology team\nprovides comprehensive supportive care, including\npain management\nand nutritional guidance, tailored to your pet’s specific needs. We’ll work closely with you to ensure they enjoy the best possible quality of life. And when the time comes to say goodbye, we’ll offer compassionate support, helping you navigate difficult decisions and ensuring your pet’s comfort.\nArranging Veterinary Oncology Consultations\nOur comprehensive 60-minute veterinary oncology consultations are designed to provide a thorough understanding of your\npet’s condition.\nBefore your appointment, our clinicians meticulously review their medical history, imaging, and lab results. During the consultation, we’ll discuss your pet’s lifestyle and any relevant medical history, conduct a full physical examination and address your specific concerns. This allows us to create a personalised treatment plan. We can often perform necessary diagnostic tests and initiate treatment on the same day, but we also respect your need for time to consider your options. For added convenience, we offer virtual consultations for initial discussions.\nRefer your oncology case today here\nIf you require more information on our\nVeterinary Oncology services\n, reach out to the team at Davies today.\nElectrochemotherapy is a key component of our Oncology Care. Learn more in our\nelectrochemotherapy factsheet\n.\nSee all our services\nRefer a case\nOncology Fact Sheets\nOur Fact Sheets provide in depth information on different cancers and the therapies available.\nRead More\nOncology Nursing at Davies\nA day in the life of our Oncology nurses.\nWatch Video\nOncology at Davies\nWatch our video to learn more about our Oncology team.\nWatch Video\nOncology Case Studies\nSee the most recent cases treated by our team of Veterinary Oncology specialists and clinicians.\nRead More\nOncology Patient Journey\nJoin Scrappy Nelson for a 'behind-the-scenes' look at a visit to our Oncology team.\nWatch Video\nElectrochemotherapy\nElectrochemotherapy is a novel cancer treatment that, thanks to its versatility, is gaining popularity in the field of veterinary oncology.\nRead More\nMeet the Team\nMark Goodfellow\nRCVS-recognised Specialist in Veterinary Oncology\nHead of Oncology Service\nMA VetMB DPhil CertVR DSAM DipECVIM-CA MRCVS\nDiplomate of the European College of Veterinary Internal Medicine\nRead More\nDaniela Andrade\nRegistered Veterinary Nurse - Oncology\nRead More\nSarah Benjamin\nOncology Clinician\nVMD DipACVIM (Oncology) MRCVS\nDiplomate of the American College of Internal Medicine (Oncology)\nRead More\nEllie Davis\nOncology Technician\nAnimal Care and Management - levels 1 and 2\nRead More\nEmily-Jo Moynihan\nRegistered Veterinary Nurse - Oncology\nRead More\nAmy Norton\nRegistered Veterinary Nurse - Oncology\nRead More\nPetros Odatzoglou\nRCVS-recognised Specialist in Veterinary Oncology\nDVM, MSc (Clin Onc), Dip. ECVIM-CA (Oncology), MRCVS\nRead More\nLuca Schiavo\nRCVS-recognised Specialist in Veterinary Oncology\nDVM, Dip ECVIM-CA (Onc), MRCVS\nDiplomate of the European College of Veterinary Oncology\nRead More\nRebecca Wade\nRegistered Veterinary Nurse - Oncology\nBSc (Hons)\nRead More\n\"They've provided great cancer care for my dog.\"\nKeep up to Date\nWhy choose Davies Veterinary Specialists? Recognised as ‘Outstanding’ for Client Service and Sustainability\nRecognised as ‘Outstanding’ in Client Service and Sustainability, discover what sets Davies Veterinary Specialists apart.\nRead More\nDavies Performs Rare Partial Limb Amputation\nVeterinary experts at Davies Veterinary Specialists have performed their first partial limb amputation to be subsequently fitted with a stump socket prosthesis.\nRead More\nErnie’s oncology story\nErnie is referred to our Oncology team with multiple mast cell tumours.\nRead More\nRelated Links\nSpecialist Pet Cancer Care\n|\nAnimal Cancer Specialist\n|\nVeterinary Oncologist\n|\nAnimal Referral Centre\n|\nVets Specialists\nNeed to make a referral?\nGet in touch with us using the form below.\nRefer Now\nAnaesthesia\nCardiology\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nPet Hearing Assessment Clinic\nInternal Medicine\nVeterinary Neurology and Neurosurgery\nVeterinary Nursing\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nOrthopaedics\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nTherapy and Fitness Services\nVeterinary Client Care\nAbout Us\nDavies Veterinary Specialists FAQs\nJoin Our Team\nSustainability\nLinnaeus Veterinary Limited trading as Davies Veterinary Specialists\nManor Farm Business Park\n|\nHigham Gobion\n|\nHertfordshire\n|\nSG5 3HR\n|\nTel 01582 883950\nRegistered address: Friars Gate 1011 Stratford Road Solihull B90 4BN\n|\nRegistered in England & Wales 10790375\n|\nVAT Reg 195 092 877\nCookie Settings\n© 2026 Davies Veterinary Specialists,\nPart of Linnaeus, an Affiliate of Mars, Incorporated\nHosting and Maintenance by Clickingmad\nTerms of Service (New)\nTerms of Service (Old)\nLegal Notice\nPrivacy Statement\nCookies Policy\nModern Slavery Act\nCustomer Charter\nComplaints\nGender Pay Gap Report\nAccessibility\nLinnaeus Veterinary Limited trading as Davies Veterinary Specialists\n01582 883950\n©2026 Davies Veterinary Specialists",
